 detailed, with the inference and learning procedures described step-by-step, including the specific update rules for expert means, variances, and expertise levels. The writing is concise and readable, making it easy for an expert reader to follow the methodology and reproduce the results.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-003","SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. Key variables such as the latent state h, the data point x, and the expert distributions P_k are clearly introduced and used consistently throughout the paper. The equations are well-explained, with each step of the derivation or update rule clearly stated. For example, the smoothed composition rule in Equation (4) is clearly defined, and the update rules for expert means and variances in Equations (5) and (6) are well-explained. The notation for the levels of expertise e_k and the mixture weights r_k(d) is also clearly defined and used consistently.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The figure captions are detailed and provide clear textual descriptions of the visual content. For example, the caption for Figure 1 explains that each panel shows the probabilities of the 10 experts for the 10 dimensions, with white/black corresponding to mu_k(d) = 0/1. The caption for Figure 3 describes the left panel as showing expert probabilities and the right panel as showing levels of expertise, with blue/red corresponding to small/large values. The captions for Figures 4, 5, 6, 7, and 8 similarly provide clear textual descriptions of the visual content, including the specific data points, reconstructions, and expert opinions shown. The figure references in the text are consistent with the captions, and the figures are well-integrated into the narrative.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"e33300c1f5ed7451e88649e4a105c3b3816b121771c41c53cb480095f46badfc","paper_id":"BJ46w6Ule","paper_ordinal":19,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"1858fe567275039da7432e9da01fb9ba70df6ec79a55bbfc377219228b7c297d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ46w6Ule","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"74aa5d8e1b13bf5c71312f9ad11eb93089d3ee475327be0236cc08ec0691e68a","request_identity_sha256":"5de7610483c87723d59d1a1463ac16f498136b78f8fc46410759dc806847b77f","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1108,"prompt_tokens":14936,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":16044},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"5de7610483c87723d59d1a1463ac16f498136b78f8fc46410759dc806847b77f","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}